    "result_text": "All tests green. The build's only test class is `AcceptanceTest` (3 tests), and it passes along with the full compile of the generated DTOs.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed telephone handling to store and compare numbers in **E.164** form.\n\n**New helper** \u2014 `rest/function/owner/OwnerTelephone.java`: `toE164(String)` strips spaces/dashes/brackets, keeps a leading `+` and its country code, otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0`, then requires 8\u201315 digits after the `+` (throwing `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2192 400 otherwise). E.g. `0412 345 678` \u2192 `+61412345678`, `+64 21 123 456` \u2192 `+6421123456`, `12` \u2192 rejected.\n\n**Wired it in:**\n- `RequireOwnerFields` (POST): replaced the old strip-to-10-digits rule with `OwnerTelephone.toE164`.\n- `ApplyOwner` (PUT): now normalizes to E.164 too, so both create and update store the canonical form.\n- `RequireUniqueTelephone`: duplicate detection now compares E.164 values (request is already E.164; existing owners are normalized leniently for comparison).\n\n**Constraints updated to accept E.164:**\n- `model/Owner.java`: telephone `@Pattern` changed to `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$` (removed the 10-digit `@Digits`/pattern) \u2014 needed because JPA validates the entity on persist.\n- `resources/openapi.yml`: relaxed the DTO telephone pattern/example so the `@Valid` PUT path accepts raw and E.164 input.\n\nDoc comments on `RequireOwnerFields`, `RequireUniqueTelephone`, and `InvalidTelephoneException` were updated to describe the E.164 behaviour rather than the old ten-digit rule.\n\nOne note: the PUT pipeline still doesn't run a uniqueness check (it never did) \u2014 the spec's duplicate-by-E.164 requirement lives on the create path, matching the pre-existing design.",
